course: dictionary
lesson: 10830
title: Venom
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Venom is a poison that an animal puts into another creature by biting or stinging. Snakes, spiders, scorpions and bees all use it. Look for clues in the sentence to check the meaning. «Never suck a snake bite or cut it: it does not get the venom out and it causes more harm.» Here, venom is something inside a bite that can cause harm, and sucking the bite will not remove it.
explain: Venom can also describe words. «Her voice was full of venom as she shouted at the referee.» A voice cannot hold poison, so the clue is the word shouted. The meaning is very strong, nasty anger or hate. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Try your meaning in the sentence to check it makes sense.
explain: The word is often used in two ways. In science, it is a poison a creature injects. In stories, it shows a cruel or hateful feeling. «Venomous» is the adjective: a venomous snake has venom. «Antivenom» is medicine that doctors make to treat bites.
fact: Venom is a poison that some animals inject by biting or stinging.
fact: Animals like snakes, spiders, scorpions and bees can have venom.
fact: «Venomous» means having venom, so a venomous snake can inject its poison through fangs.
fact: «Full of venom» means full of very strong, nasty anger or hate.
fact: «Antivenom» is medicine doctors make to treat bites from venomous animals.
fact: Never touch or pick up a snake or spider you do not know. If bitten, keep still and get help.
exercise: Venom is something an animal injects with a bite, sting or spine. Which of these animals uses venom? | A horse kicking | A cow kicking | *A snake with fangs | A tortoise walking
exercise: «Venomous snakes inject venom through fangs, mostly to catch prey, and bite people only when frightened or stepped on.» Why do venomous snakes mostly use venom? | *To catch prey | To warm up in the sun | To sing to other snakes | To keep their scales clean
exercise: «Her voice was full of venom as she shouted at the referee.» What does full of venom mean? | *Full of very strong, nasty anger | Full of soup | Full of fresh water | Full of happy songs
test: «Never suck a snake bite or cut it: it does not get the venom out and it causes more harm.» What should you never do to a snake bite? | Get help | Keep still | *Suck it
test: Which medicine do doctors make to treat bites from venomous animals? | *Antivenom | Sunscreen | Cough syrup
exam: «A honeybee's barbed sting stays in the skin and is scraped out sideways with a fingernail or card as soon as possible, because its venom sac keeps pumping while it stays in.» Why must a honeybee sting be scraped out quickly? | *Because the venom sac keeps pumping while the sting stays in | Because bees need their stings back | Because the sting can fly away | Because stings look untidy
